<Base title="Research publications — TruVector" description="Lane Vector and TruVector whitepapers by Michael Brandon Lane, InTellMe AI. Edition 5 October 2026." path="/publications">
<section class="room" style="padding-top:96px"><div class="suite suite--flagship"><p class="kicker">TruVector</p><h1 class="suite-title">Research publications</h1><p class="hero-support" style="margin-top:28px;max-width:66ch">Lane Vector and TruVector whitepapers by Michael Brandon Lane, InTellMe AI. Edition 5 October 2026.</p></div></section>
<section class="room" aria-labelledby="section-0"><div class="suite suite--flagship"><h2 class="suite-title" id="section-0">Lane Vector: signal direction, rate, and source structure</h2><p style="margin-top:24px;max-width:70ch">Projection onto an outcome, rate and acceleration with their noise, what the angle between texts carries, and dependence among origins. Each section ends in plain terms.</p><p style="margin-top:24px;max-width:70ch"><a href="/working-papers/WP-01.pdf">Read WP-01 PDF</a></p></div></section><section class="room" aria-labelledby="section-1"><div class="suite suite--flagship"><h2 class="suite-title" id="section-1">TruVector: source dependence and decisions from model readings</h2><p style="margin-top:24px;max-width:70ch">The reading step, the origin discount, the decision rule, six worked cases scored both ways, the first comparison on 60 statements, and eight research directions with the result that would disprove each.</p><p style="margin-top:24px;max-width:70ch"><a href="/working-papers/WP-02.pdf">Read WP-02 PDF</a></p></div></section><section class="room" aria-labelledby="section-2"><div class="suite suite--flagship"><h2 class="suite-title" id="section-2">Lane Vector and TruVector: the research in plain language</h2><p style="margin-top:24px;max-width:70ch">Written for a reader with no background: the problem, the three questions a count cannot answer, what has been measured, and what is measured next.</p><p style="margin-top:24px;max-width:70ch"><a href="/working-papers/WP-03.pdf">Read WP-03 PDF</a></p></div></section><section class="room" aria-labelledby="section-4"><div class="suite suite--flagship"><h2 class="suite-title" id="section-4">Counting shared words against reading meaning: Study TV-001</h2><p style="margin-top:24px;max-width:70ch">300 statements with sourced labels, four readers from four companies, one set of stored replies scored two ways. The plan written in advance, the full tables, the weak spot on recent events, and what the study does not show.</p><p style="margin-top:24px;max-width:70ch"><a href="/publications/word-overlap-vs-meaning">Read the study page</a> &middot; <a href="/working-papers/WP-04.pdf">Read WP-04 PDF</a></p></div></section><section class="room" aria-labelledby="section-3"><div class="suite suite--flagship"><h2 class="suite-title" id="section-3">Lane Vector and TruVector validation framework</h2><p style="margin-top:24px;max-width:70ch">How each measurement is made, what passing means, and what is recorded so that someone else can repeat it.</p><p style="margin-top:24px;max-width:70ch"><a href="/working-papers/Validation-framework.pdf">Read Validation-framework PDF</a></p></div></section>
<section class="room"><div class="suite suite--flagship"><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="/publications">Read the research papers</a><a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/investors#request">Discuss a solution</a></div></div></section>
</Base>
